From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 14:02:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 36/36] calendar: Calendar message type, index of events, query
 + make events
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

iCalendar attachments (`.ics` files and the `text/calendar` part of email
invitations) become a message type of their own, `Viewtype::Calendar`,
wired like `Vcard`:

- the `.ics` suffix upgrades File on send and on draft, receiving maps
  `text/calendar` to it, and both check the content: without an event the
  message stays a File. `Summary1` carries the first event's title, so the
  chat list shows "📅 Title". On the wire it is still a plain text/calendar
  attachment; other clients see a file.
- numbered 7000, far from upstream's 10..90, so a future upstream viewtype
  can't collide with it in the database.

Events are parsed via the `icalendar` crate, recurrence via `rrule` (+
chrono-tz), and indexed in `slothfulchat_calendar_events` so the UI can query
a date range without reading every blob, and reminders can later work
natively. One row per VEVENT; recurring series are stored as a serialized
RRuleSet and expanded per query. TZIDs: IANA names, Mozilla-style path
prefixes, a table of common Windows names (Outlook/Exchange), then the
VTIMEZONE's fixed standard offset. All-day and floating times are wall-clock
encoded as UTC and flagged. Per (UID, RECURRENCE-ID) the highest SEQUENCE
(then newest message) wins; METHOD:CANCEL / STATUS:CANCELLED mark it
cancelled, RECURRENCE-ID overrides replace their occurrence.

Fork tables carry a `slothfulchat_` prefix and are created with IF NOT EXISTS
on open rather than in upstream's numbered migrations (a fork migration
number would collide with upstream's next one). They are derived data.

Deletion in every form: before each read and in housekeeping, entries of
messages that are deleted or in trash are dropped — delete for me / for
everyone, ephemeral timers, delete_device_after, chat deletion (INSERT OR
REPLACE into trash), tombstone pruning — and reads only join messages
outside trash anyway; msgs.id is AUTOINCREMENT, so ids never come back.
Not triggers: native backup import (sqlcipher_export) copies triggers into
sqlite_master without the connection knowing, so re-creating them on open
made the schema malformed, and they would travel in backups. Drafts, blocked
chats and unaccepted contact requests stay out of the calendar.

Indexed on receive and send; older messages, attachments downloaded later
and plain-File .ics (retyped to Calendar) are picked up on the next read or
in housekeeping.

JSON-RPC: `Calendar` viewtype and `calendar_event` (first event) on
MessageObject; get_calendar_events(chat?, from, to), get_calendar_chats(),
get_calendar_msg_events(msg) and make_calendar_ics(event), which writes the
.ics to send or draft as a Calendar message (like make_vcard).
